# Tracked-file attributes.
#
# claude-mem-strip filter: removes auto-appended <claude-mem-context>...</claude-mem-context>
# blocks from a tracked file before staging or comparing against HEAD. The block
# is injected by the claude-mem plugin's PostToolUse hook
# (~/.claude/plugins/cache/thedotmack/claude-mem/.../hooks/hooks.json), so without
# this filter the dump would land in commits whenever you run `git add` after a
# Claude Code session.
#
# The filter is opt-in per machine: each developer registers the clean command
# locally (see docs/agents/local-environment.md). On machines without the
# filter configured, git silently passes content through (required=false), so
# this attribute file is safe to commit and does not affect collaborators who
# do not use claude-mem.
AGENTS.md filter=claude-mem-strip
